;; JUnit 4 from its pinned sources (A10 of the Ghidra case study's G1 plan, GH7 (b); doc/go/BUILD.md, "Java sources by
;; module"): JUnit 4.13.2 and hamcrest-core 1.3 (with a variant of two lines javac rejects, patches/) read from their sources jars as modules (A2; bin/java-project fetch puts
;; test/java/project/maven-pins.edn's jars in the main checkout's .tmp/maven, the root $maven-pins), Arbace's own
;; runner arbace.junit.EdnRun (one EDN map a method), and tests that use what JUnit does by reflection: the lifecycle's
;; annotations, rules on annotated fields (a class rule, a chain, TestName, TemporaryFolder, ExpectedException,
;; ErrorCollector, TestWatcher), hamcrest's matchers, @RunWith(Parameterized), a timeout's thread. Each test is judged
;; by its own verdict, as written in its source: runs/all.out is what the runner prints when every verdict is the
;; designed one (the passes pass, the failures fail with the designed exception and message).
{:main-class arbace.junit.EdnRun
 :java {:release 25
        :repository "$maven-pins"
        :javac ["-Xlint:none" "-encoding" "UTF-8"]
        :modules [{:name "hamcrest-core" :artifact "org.hamcrest:hamcrest-core:1.3" :patches ["patches/hamcrest-core-1.3-javac.patch"]}
                  {:name "junit" :artifact "junit:junit:4.13.2" :deps ["hamcrest-core"] :patches ["patches/junit-4.13.2-jdk18.patch"]}
                  {:name "runner" :src ["runner/src"] :deps ["junit"]}
                  {:name "tests" :src ["tests/src"] :deps ["junit" "hamcrest-core"]}]}}
